          "description": "Role Type: Full-time\nLocation: Fully Remote\nExperience: 2–3 years\nCompensation: $700 USD base salary per month, plus up to $300 USD in performance-based bonuses per month.\nAbout the Role\nSmartPropFirm is looking for a Software Development Specialist to join our Product & Engineering team.\nYou'll build, maintain, and improve software products for the prop trading industry, including trading tools, customer dashboards, rewards systems, marketplaces, and other platform features.\nWe're looking for a skilled, proactive engineer with strong technical fundamentals, practical full-stack development experience, and the ability to independently solve problems, take ownership of features, and deliver reliable solutions using modern technologies and AI-assisted development tools.\nResponsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain features across our web platform.\nBuild scalable, maintainable, and production-ready frontend and backend solutions.\nTake ownership of features from development through testing and deployment.\nIntegrate APIs, databases, authentication systems, and third-party services.\nIdentify and resolve bugs, performance bottlenecks, and technical issues.\nWrite clean, well-structured, reusable, and thoroughly tested code.\nConduct code reviews and contribute to improving engineering practices.\nLeverage AI development tools to accelerate development, debugging, and problem-solving.\nCollaborate with product, design, and engineering teams to deliver high-quality solutions.\nRequirements\n2–3 years of professional software development experience.\nStrong programming fundamentals and problem-solving skills.\nProficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, React, Next.js, and Node.js.\nHands-on experience with full-stack web application development.\nSolid understanding of REST APIs, databases, authentication, and application architecture.\nExperience working with Git, code reviews, and collaborative development workflows.\nAbility to debug complex issues and optimize application performance.\nExperience using AI development tools such as ChatGPT, Cursor, Claude, or GitHub Copilot.\nStrong communication skills and the ability to work independently in a remote environment.\nAbility to take ownership of tasks and deliver high-quality work with minimal supervision.\nNice to Have\nFamiliarity with cloud services, CI/CD pipelines, and deployment workflows.\nUnderstanding of responsive UI/UX principles and frontend performance optimization.\nExperience with automated testing and production monitoring.\nExperience or interest in fintech, trading platforms, dashboards, marketplaces, or rewards systems.\nWhy Join SmartPropFirm?\nWork on real products used by traders.\nTake ownership of meaningful features and technical solutions.\nWork remotely with a collaborative, fast-moving team.\nBuild with modern technologies and AI-assisted development workflows.\nGain exposure to multiple products and complex engineering challenges.\nGrow professionally in an environment where your contributions have a direct impact.\nAdditional Requirements\n2-3+ years of hands-on experience with modern software engineering practices.\nStrong practical experience with Next.js and React.\nDemonstrated ability to independently develop, debug, and deliver production-ready features.\nComfortable working in a fully remote, collaborative development environment.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486308777": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T06:07:19.532152+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Overview\nCotiviti is a leading solutions and analytics company that leverages unparalleled clinical and financial datasets to deliver deep insight into the performance of the healthcare system. These insights uncover new opportunities for healthcare organizations to collaborate to improve their financial performance, reduce inefficiency, and improve healthcare quality. The healthcare landscape is rapidly changing. The Associate Software Engineer will work to deliver on projects. This person will work in a fast-paced environment where the collective team emphasis is to generate market driven solutions that work. The successful candidate will be required to collaborate effectively with developers, offshore development team members, business owners, project management, and other internal stakeholders. We develop highly innovative customer-facing applications in healthcare analytics to generate performance, improvement opportunities, and value for our clients.\nResponsibilities\nWork within the team developing and supporting analytics systems with patent pending technology and applications to support our in-house audit partners.\nDesign and implement new solutions.\nLearn new technologies and apply them to the problem space.\nPeer review software changes by other developers.\nProvide technical guidance to the team on development.\nDocument the specifications, design, features, and operation of applications prior to production rollout.\nWork collaboratively with business partners to define and ensure the completeness and accuracy of system/technical requirements.\nComplete all responsibilities as outlined in the annual performance review and/or goal setting.\nComplete all special projects and other duties as assigned.\nMust be able to perform duties with or without reasonable accommodation.\nThis job description is intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed and is not to be construed as an exhaustive list of responsibilities, duties and skills required. This job description does not constitute an employment agreement and is subject to change as the needs of Cotiviti and requirements of the job change.\nQualifications\nBachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Information Systems or related field or equivalent work experience.\n0-1 year of industry experience.\nStrong organizational, analytical and communication skills.\nBasic understanding of software engineering principles, design principles, performance, and applications that scale.\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills.\nAbility to execute project deliverables in a dynamic, fast-paced environment within estimated timelines.\nOptimization and tuning of SQL queries, stored procedures, and triggers\n0-1 year experience with scripting languages: VBScript or PowerShell\n0-1 year experience with Java or .NET Frameworks\n0-1 year experience with Amazon Web Services (AWS)\n0-1 year experience with Microsoft SQL Server\n0-1 year experience with PostgreSQL\nBasic knowledge and application of SAFe agile practices, preferred.\nProficiency working with large data sets.\nMental Requirements\nCritical Thinking: Analyze problems objectively and make sound, data-driven decisions.\nAttention to Detail: Maintain accuracy across code, data, and deliverables.\nQuantitative Skills: Apply strong analytical and statistical methods to solve problems.\nData Interpretation: Extract actionable insights from data, metrics, and visualizations.\nCommunication: Clearly explain technical concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences.\nLearning Agility: Quickly adopt new tools, technologies, and best practices.\nResilience: Adapt to shifting priorities and deliver under pressure.\nIntegrity: Handle data responsibly and uphold engineering and ethical standards.\nPhysical Requirements And Working Conditions\nRemaining in a stationary position, often standing or sitting for prolonged periods.\nRepeating motions that may include the wrists, hands, and/or fingers.\nMust be able to provide a dedicated, secure work area.\nMust be able to provide high-speed internet access / connectivity and office setup and maintenance.\nBase compensation ranges from $77,000 to $92,000 per year. Specific offers are determined by various factors, such as experience, education, skills, certifications, and other business needs.\nCotiviti offers team members a competitive benefits package to address a wide range of personal and family needs, including medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance coverage, 401(k) savings plans, paid family leave, 9 paid holidays per year, and 17-27 days of Paid Time Off (PTO) per year, depending on specific level and length of service with Cotiviti. For information about our benefits package, please refer to our Careers page.\nThis role is based remotely and all interviews will be conducted virtually.\nDate of posting: 10/23/2026\nApplications are assessed on a rolling basis. We anticipate that the application window will close on 12/23/2026, but the application window may change depending on the volume of applications received or close immediately if a qualified candidate is selected.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487087750": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T06:07:19.532152+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the job\nMeeBoss is sharing this active opportunity on behalf of Voltus, a leading company for Distributed Energy Resources (DERs) that aims to be the platform fulfilling the promise of the energy transition.\nThis role is appropriate for entry-level to early-career engineering candidates eager to build scalable software for Voltus.\nYou will join a fully remote team tackling complex energy industry challenges, collaborating with experienced engineers on a modern tech stack, and contributing to core systems that decarbonize the grid.\nJob title\nSoftware Engineer\nCompany\nMeeBoss\nLocation\nRemote\nCompensation\nBase pay is $110,000-$140,000 USD annually, commensurate with experience, with a 10% annual bonus and equity.\nWhy this role\nJoin a fully remote team distributed across the US, Canada, and abroad.\nContribute to core systems that decarbonize the grid and provide flexibility, reliability, and resilience to the energy market.\nCollaborate with experienced engineers on a modern tech stack including Python, Postgres, Go, FastAPI, and React.\nWhat you will do\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-tested code to support the team’s projects.\nContribute to the design and implementation of new features and services.\nCollaborate with your team to troubleshoot and resolve issues in the production environment.\nParticipate in code reviews to learn from and contribute to the team’s shared knowledge.\nWork with stakeholders to understand requirements and translate them into technical solutions.\nWhat we are looking for\nA Bachelor’s degree, or equivalent combination of education and experience, in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.\nFoundational programming skills in a backend language like Python.\nA strong desire to learn and grow as a software engineer.\nExcellent communication and collaboration skills.\nA genuine passion for creating a cleaner, more resilient energy future.\nAuthorization to work in the US or Canada without sponsorship.\nA link to your GitHub account in the application (applications without a GitHub account will not be considered).\nBenefits\nUnlimited PTO for full-time employees.\nParental leave.\nComprehensive benefits package to promote health, wellness, and financial security.\nAbout MeeBoss\nMeeBoss helps job seekers and hiring teams make direct, relevant career connections.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487099185": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T06:07:19.532152+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Position Description & Qualifications\nWe are seeking a Junior Software Engineer to support a DoD program. The candidate will work with the technical lead and development team to maintain and enhance existing Java-based applications in the cloud environment, troubleshoot issues, and support ongoing development and modernization efforts. The position offers opportunities to learn Python, APEX and other application development tools, as well as gain hands-on experience to AI-assisted development practices already being used by the team. Prior experience with AI technologies is not required, we are looking for someone with a solid Java foundation, strong problem-solving skills, and a willingness to learn new technologies. The candidate will be a self-starter, team-player and will be expected to manage and complete their tasks in a fast-paced results driven environment.\nThis position is fully remote, and candidates may be located anywhere within the United States. Candidates must have an interim or active Secret security clearance.\nIn This Role, You Will\nContribute to all phases of the development lifecycle.\nWrite well designed, testable, and efficient code.\nCode, design, and implement Java and APEX solutions for the Army.\nConduct software analysis, programming, testing, debugging activities and maintenance.\nDevelop technical designs for application development and recommend changes to improve established application processes.\nTo Be Successful In This Role, You Must Have\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science.\nAn interim or active Secret security clearance.\n1 year of relevant IT experience.\nExperience with software development lifecycle.\nExperience with Java software design, development, testing, and deployment.\nExperience with web-based applications, client/server applications, or cloud-hosted systems.\nAbility to travel 10%.\nAdditional Desired Qualifications\nExperience with software development concepts and Agile methodologies.\nExperience with common release tracking software (JIRA, Confluence).\nExperience with basic SQL.\nKnowledge of AWS Cloud.\nKnowledge of leveraging AI-assisted development tools, automated code generation, or AI-powered engineering capabilities.\nIf you are interested in working with a dedicated Serco team, then submit your application now for immediate consideration. It only takes a few minutes!\nCompany Overview\nSerco Inc. (Serco) is the Americas division of Serco Group, plc. In North America, Serco’s 9,000+ employees strive to make an impact every day across 100+ sites in the areas of Defense, Citizen Services, and Transportation. We help our clients deliver vital services more efficiently while increasing the satisfaction of their end customers. Serco serves every branch of the U.S. military, numerous U.S. Federal civilian agencies, the Intelligence Community, the Canadian government, state, provincial and local governments, and commercial clients. While your place may look a little different depending on your role, we know you will find yours here. Wherever you work and whatever you do, we invite you to discover your place in our world. Serco is a place you can count on and where you can make an impact because every contribution matters.\nTo review Serco benefits please visit: https://careers.serco-na.com/us/en/what-we-offer. If you require an accommodation with the application process please email: careers@serco-na.com or call the HR Service Desk at 800-628-6458, option 1. Please note, due to EEOC/OFCCP compliance, Serco is unable to accept resumes by email.\nCandidates may be asked to present proof of identity during the selection process. If requested, this will require presentation of a government-issued I.D. (with photo) with name and address that match the information entered on the application. Serco will not take possession of or retain/store the information provided as proof of identity. For more information on how Serco uses your information, please see our Applicant Privacy Policy and Notice.\nSerco does not accept unsolicited resumes through or from search firms or staffing agencies without being a contracted approved vendor. All unsolicited resumes will be considered the property of Serco and will not be obligated to pay a placement or contract fee. If you are interested in becoming an approved vendor at Serco, please email Agencies@serco-na.com.\nSerco is an equal opportunity employer. We evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics.\nPay Transparency\nOur Total Rewards package includes competitive pay, performance-based incentives, and benefits that promote well-being and work-life balance—so you can thrive both professionally and personally. Eligible employees also gain access to a wide range of benefits from comprehensive health coverage and health savings accounts to retirement plans, life and disability insurance, and time-off programs that support work-life balance. Program availability may vary based on factors such as contract type, location, hire date, and applicable collective bargaining agreements.\nSalary range: The range for this position can be found at the top of this posting. This range is provided as a general guideline and represents a good faith estimate across all experience levels. Actual base salary will be determined by a variety of factors, including but not limited to, the scope of the role, relevant experience, job-related knowledge, education and training, key skills, and geographic market considerations. For roles available in multiple states, the range may vary to reflect differences in local labor markets. In addition to base salary, eligible positions may include other forms of compensation such as annual bonuses or long-term incentive opportunities. Benefits – Comprehensible benefits for full-time employees (part-time employees receive a limited package tailored to their role):\nMedical, dental, and vision insurance\nRobust vacation and sick leave benefits, and flexible work arrangements where permitted by role or contract\n401(k) plan that includes employer matching funds\nTuition reimbursement program\nLife insurance and disability coverage\nOptional coverages that can be purchased, including pet insurance, home and auto insurance, additional life and accident insurance, critical illness insurance, group legal, ID theft protection\nBirth, adoption, parental leave benefits\nEmployee Assistance Plan\nTo review all Serco benefits please visit: https://careers.serco-na.com/us/en/about-us.\nSerco complies with all applicable state and local leave laws, including providing time off under the Colorado Healthy Families and Workplaces Act for eligible Colorado residents, in alignment with our policies and benefit plans. The application window for this position is for no more than 60 days. We encourage candidates to apply promptly after the posting date, as the position may close earlier if filled or if the application volume exceeds expectations. Please submit applications exclusively through Serco’s external (or internal) career site. If an applicant has any concerns with job posting compliance, please send an email to: careers@serco-na.com.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
