        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T06:07:19.532152+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Role\nThe company is seeking an Entry-Level Software Engineer to design, develop, and maintain software solutions in a fully remote work environment. Working under the guidance of experienced engineers, you will contribute to software development projects while building your technical skills and gaining practical experience.\nThis role involves writing clean and efficient code, supporting back-end web services and APIs, participating in code reviews, debugging issues, and assisting with testing and deployment. You will also collaborate with cross-functional teams, document technical work, and learn to work with new technologies as part of a distributed engineering team.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain software solutions under the guidance of experienced engineers.\nWrite clean, efficient, and maintainable code.\nParticipate in code reviews and apply feedback to improve code quality.\nDebug software issues and contribute to identifying and implementing solutions.\nSupport the development of back-end web services and APIs.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to understand project requirements.\nDocument technical work and development processes.\nAssist with software testing and deployment activities.\nLearn and adapt to new technologies, tools, and development practices.\nContribute to company projects while developing software engineering skills.\nRequired Qualifications\nFoundational knowledge of computer science concepts, including algorithms, data structures, and software engineering principles.\nUnderstanding of software development and programming, with experience in at least one modern programming language such as Java, C#, Python, or JavaScript.\nUnderstanding of Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts and the ability to apply them in practical code.\nExposure to back-end web development, including APIs, databases, and server-side frameworks.\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.\nAbility to work remotely, manage time effectively, and collaborate through online communication and project management tools.\nStrong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\nWillingness to learn, accept feedback, and develop technical skills through mentorship.\nPreferred Qualifications\nBasic knowledge of version control systems such as Git.\nFamiliarity with software development lifecycle practices.\nWork Arrangement\nFull-time position.\nFully remote work environment.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T06:07:19.532152+00:00"
  },
